-902c-a4cd-4d80"}],"description":"## Observation\n\n`make verify` on 2026-11-16 (worktree at b4e0d01b6491 plus an unrelated MCP change; load average 17-44 from concurrent verifies on the host) failed exactly 1 of 21,307 default-tier tests:\n\n`tests/scripts/test_observability_interrupt_reasons.py::test_each_reason_counter_keeps_its_own_offset` raised `subprocess.TimeoutExpired`: `bash infra/scripts/observability.sh` exceeded the test's `run_observability(..., timeout=60)` bound.\n\nRerun alone on the same tree at load ~11: all 5 tests in the file passed in 43.7 s wall (2 min 04 s including collection), so a single script invocation runs within a factor of a few of the 60 s bound even on a moderately loaded host.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n\n- The fixed 60 s wall-clock bound is too tight for `observability.sh` under host load (the script forks many subprocesses).\n- The script blocks on some host resource under load (journal read, process spawn) that the test isolation in edf66bc13a0 does not stub.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Root-cause the timeout with a deterministic reproduction (e.g. constrained CPU) and record the cause here.\n- [ ] Fix the class so the test does not depend on host load to pass, without adding a config key, env var or flag.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b2ad0f89-8899-4b86-bb9c-09bb6ced9cd8","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["flaky","tests","observability"],"ticket_id":"bd8d-54e9-682f-46a3","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_each_reason_counter_keeps_its_own_offset times out at 60 s under host load in make verify","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5c788dbe-263c-4148-b343-28132756b6b